        'Optimists envisage a symbiosis rather than a replacement. Augmented by intelligent tools, they argue, humans will be freed from drudgery to pursue creative, relational and strategic work. A radiologist assisted by software may diagnose more accurately than either could alone; a teacher relieved of marking may devote more attention to each child. On this view, technology does not make people obsolete; it makes them more fully human. Transhumanists go further still, imagining implants that augment memory, interfaces that connect brains to networks and, eventually, minds that transcend biology altogether.',
