      model: 'In the usual language, my country\'s currency has "plummeted" amid "jittery" markets, and the central bank is "battling" inflation that is "spiralling out of control". In more literal terms: investors have sold the currency because the government increased spending without raising revenue, and import prices have risen as a result. The metaphorical version makes it sound like a natural disaster. The literal version shows that specific policy choices, and specific people, were involved — which is far more useful if we want to discuss solutions.',
